<title>USA: U.S. May durable goods orders fell 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. May durable goods orders fell 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	May     Apr--Rev from     Mar</p>
<p>  New Orders		 -0.6     1.8     1.3	-2.8</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.  -3.3     2.8     3.4	-4.8</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.     0.2     1.6     0.5	-2.2</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	-0.1     1.1     0.6	-2.4</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders    -12.8    27.5    26.5     -14.7</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders   0.7    -1.7    -1.8	-3.8</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts    0.6    -1.5    -1.3	-1.7</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    May	Apr---Rev from     Mar</p>
<p> New Orders		176.10   177.16   176.16    173.94</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  38.41    39.71    39.92     38.62</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   137.68   137.44   136.19    135.33</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     170.63   170.88   169.33    169.02</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	5.47     6.27     6.22	4.92</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  44.02    43.74    43.72     44.51</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   38.79    38.56    38.64     39.16</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	May     Apr--Rev from     Mar</p>
<p> Total Shipments	   -1.2     1.3     1.2	 0.8</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders    UNCH   -0.3    -0.4	-0.5</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    May	Apr---Rev from     Mar</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 176.32   178.51   178.33    176.22</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   496.46   496.68   495.87    498.04</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES   May     Apr--Rev from     Mar</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	   -2.4     2.3     2.4	 0.4</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery   -1.0     2.9     2.9	-0.9</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery   10.4    -3.2    -6.3	-6.1</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  15.4ypppp  15.89     15.52</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  33.52    33.84   33.84     32.89</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  30.80    27.90   26.99     28.81</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected May durable goods orders to rise 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>The department said the 1.2 percent decline in shipments last month was the first this year and that order backlogs have been unchanged or down for three straight months.  </p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    May	Apr---Rev from     Mar</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 176.32   178.51   178.33    176.22</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   496.46   496.68   495.87    498.04</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES   May     Apr--Rev from     Mar</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	   -2.4     2.3     2.4	 0.4</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery   -1.0     2.9     2.9	-0.9</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery   10.4    -3.2    -6.3	-6.1</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:   Primary Metals	  15.49    15.88   16.45     15.52</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  33.52    33.84   33.84     32.89</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  30.80    27.90   26.99     28.81</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected May durable goods orders to rise 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>The department said the 1.2 percent decline in shipments last month was the first this year and that order backlogs have been unchanged or down for three straight months.</p>
